{"game": "space-marine-2011", "language": "english", "appid": 55150, "month": "2026-10", "window": 2, "start_date": 1791417600, "end_date": 1792108799, "month_true_total": 25, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 18:09:05 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "237295653", "author": {"steamid": "76561197963999749", "personaname": "Keftsmaell", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Keftsmaell/", "num_games_owned": 4493, "num_reviews": 215, "playtime_forever": 786, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 524, "playtime_at_review": 786, "deck_playtime_at_review": 775, "last_played": 1791561102, "avatar": "f1a991d19024090c3a51e96067316ff29595a8bb"}, "language": "english", "review": "\"SPACE MARINE!\"\n- everyone, all the time\n\nIt's repetitive and lacks finesse, level and environmental design is quite uninspired and monotonous, weapons are unbalanced, dodging is a bit awkward and it moves slow (lore-wise kind of fitting, but a bit of a hassle sometimes).\n\nIt's quite a fun Ork stomper in the end though. For a while. It does nothing really new, or even amazingly well, but if you're into a brain dead Gears of War-like from a bygone era; it might be up your alley. The story is decent and fits the game's vibe good enough. The last third is a bit of a drag, but it's not a very long game so it's fine.\n\nWorked like a charm on the Steam Deck. I played it maxed out on a docked one without any issues.", "timestamp_created": 1791561928, "timestamp_updated": 1791562290, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": true, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "237248519", "author": {"steamid": "76561198034441655", "personaname": "Bob Rossman", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198034441655/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 108, "playtime_forever": 65, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 65, "playtime_at_review": 65, "last_played": 1791506664, "avatar": "338a3225a31ca7ae2411bbf1d80c29129df54541"}, "language": "english", "review": "Yes. For The Emperor!", "timestamp_created": 1791507053, "timestamp_updated": 1791507053, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "237211307", "author": {"steamid": "76561198080081255", "personaname": "RoxiModifier", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/RoxiModifier/", "num_games_owned": 363, "num_reviews": 106, "playtime_forever": 156, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 156, "playtime_at_review": 92, "last_played": 1791525792, "avatar": "eeb589ee9c3a8f9fa643459ce9de11a854f4c7e5"}, "language": "english", "review": "This is a game that is held back entirely by the fact that it's an XBox 360 3rd Person Shooter aping off of the success of Gears of War.\nSomehow, they managed to make a Forge World in the midst of an Ork Invasion look brown and boring! It's crazy.\nAnd yet, the game desperately WANTS to be more than that, and does everything in its power to do so. The combat is engaging, the glory kills are fun, and it has no press button to go behind cover mechanics.\nAnd the Orks do go \"waaagh\" so basically 10/10?", "timestamp_created": 1791472122, "timestamp_updated": 1791472122, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "237198893", "author": {"stea